Z||000007||Formula88||12-21-2001||11:28 AM||||The white room on Pad 39A at Kennedy Space Center or the VAB at KSC.  Pretty much <I>anywhere</I> I've worked at KSC would count, I guess.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The view from the top of the Shuttle on the pad is breathtaking.  And the inside of the VAB, well, that's my cathedral.  I can't imagine another building being as awe-inspiring.  It's so big, that when the temperature changes quickly, you can get cloud formations <B>inside</B> the building.<P>To date, that's the only job I've ever had where I leapt out of bed at 5:30A.M. excited about going to work!  And I'm a night person!||||reg||14
Z||000008||Rodrv6||12-21-2001||11:28 AM||||Prague, Czech Rebublic!!!  Was there at Christmas last year.  Very cool (temp in the teens) and a really neat city.  It's on my list of places to go back too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||10
Z||000009||Philphine||12-21-2001||11:35 AM||||spent one day in paris (day trip from germany) nice.  <P>egypt, but a terrorist bombing just before we were scheduled to go restricted our touring/sight seeing severly. got to see the pyrimids though.<P>oman. nice. nothing like you'd think the middle east would be. supposivly the king there wants tourism so no terrorist factions are allowed there. we roamed pretty freely.<P>and while it's not really exotic, i like savannah, ga. warm, beaches, the riverwalks a good place to hang out, and you don't have to learn a new language.<P>all guard trips.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>ain't no place like home,<BR>ain't no place like home,<BR>ain't no place like home.||||reg||1
