Z||000028||Fformula88||12-21-2001||04:43 PM||||Been to lotsa cool places in the US, but I'd have to choose Wrigley Field in Chicago.  I am a huge baseball junkie, a die-hard Cubs fan (and they kill me every year!) and just cannot spend enough time there!  I also love going to Hawaii, Pheonix, and Washington DC.  Hawaii is neat because its got just about every climate... tropics obviously but up in the mountains and volcanoes there is snow, regular trees, desert areas.  All on such a little Island!||||reg||1
Z||000029||PAUL88GT||12-21-2001||05:01 PM||||For people watching it would be hard to beat Venice Beach and Santa Monica in LA.<P>Banff Alberta Canada is one of the most scenic places I have seen.<P>London had the neatest old architecture I have seen, especially near the Parliment and Big Ben.<P>KSC in Florida is neat also.  I have seen four night Shuttle launches and one landing. My job requires delivering small payloads to the Shuttle processing facility about 24 hours before it launches.  <p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 12-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||GOLDSE||12-21-2001||05:10 PM||||Having a military background as well, I spent some time overseas.<P>My favorite place was Hawaii.  But I traveled to Japan, Korea, Guam, the Philipines, and Thailand.  Not to mention Panama, and Honduras.  Bangkok was definitely worth the trip.||||reg||1
